    "name": "default",
    "note": "test-dev as found: Warlock DPS, single target, 60s, all effects on. Mount figures were retargeted for #286: the sheet stored them pre-multiplied by max bolster and rounded inconsistently at source (item level 1750*2.25 = 3937.5 truncated to 3937, combined rating 1575*2.25 = 3543.75 rounded up to 3544). The engine scales unrounded base values and lands on the exact products, so the expectations here are those products -- the sheet's own arithmetic, carried out without its rounding. Only values that actually disagreed were touched, and every one was within the offset those two source roundings can account for; the companion values, which divide exactly by 2.2, needed no change at all. Everything still has to reproduce to 1e-6. Expectations were later rebased onto the engine after the combat enchantment item levels were halved and their outgoing damage moved from a multiplicative to an additive stat: item level feeds the rating-to-percent conversion, so every percentage stat, cap, overcap and derived total shifted with it."
